+Opaque/no-evaluator symbols imported by the supplied fixed semantics:
+
+float.k:
+intFloatDiv, divII, floatMod, floatLt, absF, subF, divF, addF, mulF,
+powF, gtF, eqF, decStrToF, divFloatIntV, intToF, truncF, roundF, roundFN,
+sqrtF.
+
+sort.k:
+sortVS, sortKeyVS.
+
+builtins.k:
+md5hexCodes.
+
+Additional supplied functions described as opaque on symbolic arguments:
+strLt, floorFI, toF, ceilF, valSeqAt.
+
+Reachability assessment:
+The submitted constructor tree contains no Float, Str, list, sorted, subscript,
+math call, hashlib call, or corresponding bound/builtin operation. The fixed
+dispatch rules therefore cannot construct any of these symbols on the theorem's
+path. None occurs in verification.k or spec.k, so none affects a guard, state,
+return value, or postcondition in any target claim.
diff --git a/evidence/stage1_integrity.sh b/evidence/stage1_integrity.sh
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..2971680867b2c753746a4b6254f368f3b4a0e0e0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/evidence/stage1_integrity.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,145 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env bash
+set +e
+
+run() {
+  printf 'COMMAND: %s\n' "$*"
+  "$@"
+  local status=$?
+  printf 'EXIT STATUS: %s\n' "$status"
+}
+
+run sha256sum \
+  /audit-input.json \
